Usage: ms map <file.ms|ms.toml> [--view <view>] [--entity name] [--depth n] [--diff <file|->] [--format name] [-o output] [--json]

Show the structure of a checked program. Every view reads the same checked source; ms never runs git.
--view picks the question:
  calls (default), overview, effects, errors, modules, flow, scope, tasks, types, ownership
                  A static call graph of project declarations (standard calls are boundary leaves), as the tree for one question.
  review          A fixed-template report of where to look: the public surface, entry points with effects, error types,
                  resources and imports, or, with --diff, the semantic effect of a change.
  inspect         Checked symbols, source hashes, call sites, and statement spans as JSON.

Call graph views (the default and every --view except review and inspect):
overview (modules, their effects and cross-module calls), calls (who is called), effects (where effects enter),
errors (error types and try sites), modules (imports), flow (one function's ordered steps), scope (its cleanup scopes and exits),
tasks (its task groups and the work each spawn starts), types (aliases: class; fields and cases that hold other types),
ownership (alias: mutability; checked copy, borrow, move and var parameters; owned or borrowed results).
flow, scope and tasks need --entity. --entity roots the tree at one declaration (name, qualified name, file::name, or an exact entity ID,
which takes precedence; a path for modules) and --depth bounds expansion (default 3, at most 200 nodes).
  --entity <name>      Root the view at one declaration or module
  --depth <n>          Expansion depth for a view (default 3)
  --diff <path|->      Mark what a unified diff changed (in a view, or in the html page; the tree is the after state)
  --format <name>      ascii (default), mermaid, or html (one interactive page for the whole program)
  --json               Emit a versioned diagram tree with source IDs and locations (default: calls view)

Review (--view review): without --diff it maps the project. With a unified diff it compares the checked program before and after
the change and ranks entities by contract, effect, error-flow, and resource changes and their reach. Pipe the diff in; the tree must be
the diff's after state, and the before state is rebuilt from the diff and verified. Output is deterministic, with no timestamps,
absolute paths, or generated prose, and ends with a digest.
  --diff <path|->      Unified diff to review (- reads standard input)
  --format <name>      ascii (default) or markdown
  --json               Emit the complete report or explanation as versioned JSON (not with --format)
  --explain <n|id>     Show one finding in full: score terms, evidence, callers (needs --diff)
  --effect <pattern>   Keep findings that reach or permit this effect, e.g. std.net.* (needs --diff)
  --all                Show every row instead of the first five per section

Inspect (--view inspect): -o writes the JSON to a file (default: stdout); --json reports a failure as JSON diagnostics.

Options:
  -o, --output <path>  Write output to a file (default: stdout)
  -h, --help  Show this help without executing the command

Examples:
  ms map main.ms
  ms map ms.toml --format mermaid -o calls.mmd
  ms map ms.toml --view effects --entity save
  ms map ms.toml --view errors
  ms map ms.toml --format html -o map.html
  ms map ms.toml --view ownership --entity save
  ms map ms.toml --view flow --entity save --diff change.patch
  ms map ms.toml --view flow --entity save --json
  ms map ms.toml --view review
  git diff --no-renames main... | ms map ms.toml --view review --diff -
  ms map ms.toml --view review --diff change.patch --explain 1
  ms map ms.toml --view inspect -o inspection.json
